    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d635-a1">

                <pb facs="1019" n="1001" sameAs="frus:frus1948v03/pg1001"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lovett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Snyder</hi>)</head>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: As you know, Portuguese
                    assets in this country are still blocked. The Department of State and our
                    Embassy <pb facs="1020" n="1002" xml:id="pg1002"/> in Lisbon have recently
                    reviewed the situation and have come to the conclusion that overriding political
                    and strategic considerations of our foreign policy make it essential that
                    Portuguese assets in this country should be unblocked forthwith.</p>
                <p>I should appreciate therefore if you could give the necessary instructions to the
                    effect that Portuguese assets in the United States will be unblocked at such
                    date as may be designated by this Department with due regard to the technical
                    details of issuing the license.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d635-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert</hi> A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d635-f1" n="3" xml:id="d635-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary Snyder replied on August 31 that on September 2 an amendment would be
                    issued to General License No. 53 to include Portugal in the generally licensed
                    trade area and to unblock Portuguese assets in the United States
                    (840.51FC53/8–3148).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
